A||N||20||stimpy||Oklahoma Fiero Fest Update (LONG)||||14||
Z||000000||stimpy||05-06-2001||06:57 PM||||Okie dokie folks, here is the scoop. The 9th Annual Southwest Regional Fiero Fest is May 19th at Ferguson Pontiac in Norman OK from 10a-4p. There will be a catered BBQ (included in registration cost) following at a park TBA. It will be BYOB to keep costs down, but don't feel compelled to kick your wife out of the car so you can pack a cooler, as club members will be throwing down generously.<BR>Awards will be passed out at that time.  We will be having judging in the following classes:<BR>1. Stock coupes<BR>2. Stock Fastbacks<BR>The stock classes are to recognize the hard work and effort it takes to keep a car showroom stock. Cars in this catagory have less then 3 changes. Does not include stuff like tires or oil filters, that kinda crud. But radio, upgrades not in original RPO, or wheels will be looked at.<BR>3. Modified coupe<BR>4. Modified fastback<BR>3 or more modifications. Includes paint, exhaust, intakes, sound systems, etc. Most cars do seem to fall in to this class.<BR>5. Extreme. <BR>These cars are substantially changed from Pontiac's vision. Radical powerplant swaps, body kits, etc.<P>I could be missing some classes, but with a 1,2,3 in each class, you can see that lots o' plaques will go out. Souvenier t-shirts are also included in price of registration, just $25.<P>After our awards picnic we will caravan to Coit's Root Beer stand in OKC. Coit's is an old-school drive in that has monthly cruise-ins with LOTS of cars of every variey. It's a blast when we roll up in the Fieros. Let's roll twenty deep this year!<P>Lodging is plentiful with a Days Inn and a Holiday Inn within a mile of the show.  Look to meet me at the Days Inn to welcome all you fine folks. Please let me know if you are an out-of-towner coming to the show. Email me w/your ETA and what you'll be driving and I'll keep an eye out for you.<P><P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000001||Alex2004||05-06-2001||09:39 PM||||Hey Stimpy, my car probably won't be ready in time for the show but if something happens and it is, what class would mine fall under?  LOL... 84 SE, w/ fastback, aero front & rear fascia & g/fx GT wheel's, GT exauhst on 4 cyl, Sony Xplod CD, & kenwood speakers?  Oh, the pillar speakers too, not the ones in the seat!  hehe, just wondering.  Let me know mmkay!  Thanks, <P>Alex...  PS: we will be at the show though...||||reg||10
Z||000002||stimpy||05-06-2001||10:27 PM||||That would be the "Identity Crisis class"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Pretty sure that would go in Extreme class but possibly just modified. Good question, just the type of contraversy that makes these shows so much fun!<P>PS, Mrs stimpy says hi.<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||10
